  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Mid-Atlantic Interstate Transmission, LLC (MAIT) has authorization from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) to issue short-term debt of up to $400 million through bank facilities and FirstEnergy&amp;#x2019;s regulated money pool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;MAIT &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;has the ability to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; borrow from its regulated affiliates and FirstEnergy &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;Corp, (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;FE) to meet its short-term working capital requirements. FirstEnergy Service Company administers this money pool and tracks surplus funds of FirstEnergy and the respective regulated &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;subsidiary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, as well as proceeds available from bank borrowings. Companies receiving a loan under the money pool agreements must repay the principal amount of the loan, together with accrued interest, within 364 days of borrowing the funds. The rate of interest is the same for each company receiving a loan from their respective pool and is based on the average cost of funds available &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;through the pool. The average interest rate for borrowings for the first three months of 2026 was 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% per annum.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; font-weight:bold"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="HHDB4E63D65FD21AE5462A8FBA840EA717" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
